# Parity complete mappings and translation transversals

This is a repository-derived explicit construction in the setting of
complete mappings of finite groups. The general Hall-Paige theorem is
background, not a premise. This volume is reference input; the
repository's mathematical truth source is its Lean declaration.

For a positive integer $m$, let
$H_m=(\mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z)\times(\mathbb Z/(2m)\mathbb Z)$.
The addition table of $H_m$ has rows $x$, columns $y$, and symbol
$x+y$. A graph $\{(x,\theta(x)):x\in H_m\}$ meets each row exactly
once. It also meets each column and each symbol exactly once precisely
when both $\theta$ and $x\mapsto x+\theta(x)$ are permutations. Such a
map is a complete mapping of $H_m$.

